    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0112" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg30"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 611.3231/187.</note>
                <head>[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-01-15"><hi rendition="#italic">January 15,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Executive decree 12th grants tariff reduction during 1911 of 30 per cent, an
                        increase<anchor n="1" xml:id="d27-f1"/> on American flour and 20 per cent on
                    remaining 15 items so favored during 1910. Have submitted supplemental list, but
                    further concessions this year improbable. Conclusion of a reciprocity may be
                    proposed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dudley.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d27-f1" n="1" xml:id="d27-f1-content">
                <p>In increase of the reduction.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
